    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1237">

                <pb facs="1060" n="956" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg956"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2138.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 10, 1913.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instruction
                    No. 1447 of October 15, 1913, I have the honor to inform you that both the
                    French and Russian Governments have definitely refused to accept the proposition
                    made by the Mexican Foreign Office under date of July 22, 1913,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1237-f1"/> in the matter of the claims of their nationals against
                    Mexico growing out of the disorders therein, and have informed the present
                    administration here in this sense.</p>
                <p>In the event of my being able to procure more definite details in the premises I
                    shall forthwith inform you.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1237-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1237-f1-content">
                <p>This is the date of the meeting described in the inclosure to Mr. O’Shaughnessy’s
                    despatch of October 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
